      "parent": "cs_dos_wrap",
      "metadata": {
        "comment": "Sprint 48 decision 1: a KIT node, not Show Popup — the runtime popup has no dialog semantics, Escape or focus handling, so a graph-native reveal would regress all six of the product's accessibility properties. OpenNoodl HLT-014 makes the popup a dialog; when it lands this is a candidate for replacement, not a commitment. Its root takes no space (display: contents); the dialog portals to <body>."
